Enum      : Crosshair
Constants : 3
Short     : Cursor cross hair
Remarks   : 
___________
Name      : XY
Short     : Crosshair. The cursor has two lines: one parallel with X axis and the other parallel with Y axis.
Remarks   : 
___________
Name      : X
Short     : X hairline only. The cursor has one line parallel with X axis.
Remarks   : 
___________
Name      : Y
Short     : Y hairline only. The cursor has one line parallel with Y axis.
Remarks   : 
_____________________________________
Enum      : CursorMode
Constants : 3
Short     : Cursor mode constants
Remarks   : 
___________
Name      : Fixed
Short     : Fixed
Remarks   : 
___________
Name      : Floating
Short     : Floating
Remarks   : 
___________
Name      : Snap
Short     : Snapped to currently selected element
Remarks   : 
_____________________________________
Enum      : TrackModeState
Constants : 9
Short     : Tracking Mode constants.
Remarks   : 
___________
Name      : None
Short     : None
Remarks   : 
___________
Name      : TrackCursor
Short     : Track cursor position (Hold left mouse button pressed).
Remarks   : 
___________
Name      : TrackElement
Short     : Track element position. When the mouse is dragged having left button down, the coordinates of the <STRONG>closest</STRONG> point are displayed in a tooltip.
Remarks   : 
___________
Name      : Zoom
Short     : Zoom XY. Drag the mouse to define a rectangle for zoom. When left mouse button is released, the area enclosed in rectangle becomes the new plot area (zoom <B>in</B>).<P>To revert back just right click the mouse.
Remarks   : 
___________
Name      : ZoomX
Short     : Zoom X. Drag the mouse to define a rectangle for zoom. When left mouse button is released, the area within left/right rectangle boundaries becomes the new plot area (zoom in on X <B>only</B> ).<P>To revert back just right click the mouse.
Remarks   : 
___________
Name      : ZoomY
Short     : Zoom Y. Drag the mouse to define a rectangle for zoom. When left mouse button is released, the area within top/bottom rectangle boundaries becomes the new plot area (zoom in on Y <B>only</B> ). <P>To revert back just right click the mouse.
Remarks   : 
___________
Name      : PanXY
Short     : Pan XY. The whole plot area moves with the mouse while dragging. <P>To revert back just right click the mouse.
Remarks   : 
___________
Name      : PanX
Short     : Pan X. The whole plot area moves on X axis with the mouse while dragging. <P>To revert back just right click the mouse.
Remarks   : 
___________
Name      : PanY
Short     : Pan Y. The whole plot area moves on Y axis with the mouse while dragging. <P>To revert back just right click the mouse.
Remarks   : 
_____________________________________
